@HostAddress = http://localhost:5179

# 1. Every product: 200, 77 products
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/products

###

# 2. Only the beverages (category 1): 200, 12 products
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/products?categoryId=1

###

# 3. One product: 200, Chai
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/products/1

###

# 4. A product that doesn't exist: 404
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/products/999

###

# 5. Add a product: 201 (after Practice: Secure the App, 401: see requests 11 to 16), with its new id and a Location header. Use that id in requests 6 to 8.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Trail Mix",
  "categoryId": 3,
  "unitPrice": 4.50,
  "unitsInStock": 20,
  "discontinued": false
}

###

# 6. Change it: 204 (put the new id in the address)
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/products/78
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Trail Mix",
  "categoryId": 3,
  "unitPrice": 4.95,
  "unitsInStock": 18,
  "discontinued": false
}

###

# 7. Delete it: 204
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/products/78

###

# 8. Delete it again: 404
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/products/78

###

# 9. A product with no name: 400, with the validation errors
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "unitPrice": 4.50
}

###

# 10. Delete a product that orders still use: 409 Conflict
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/products/1

###

# Practice: Secure the App. Run Users.sql in SSMS, and set the key with user secrets, first.

# 11. Register: 200, with a token, "userName": "ada" and "role": "User" (409 if ada is taken)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "ada", "password": "summer2026" }

###

# 12. Sign in with the wrong password: 401
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "ada", "password": "summer2025" }

###

# 13. Sign in: 200, with a token
# @name login
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "ada", "password": "summer2026" }

###

# 14. Who am I: 200, ada, User
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

###

# 15. Add a product with the token: 201. Use its id in request 16.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Trail Mix",
  "categoryId": 3,
  "unitPrice": 4.50,
  "unitsInStock": 20,
  "discontinued": false
}

###

# 16. Delete it as ada: 403. Make ada an admin in SSMS, sign in again (13), and it's 204.
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/products/78
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
